3| ## Recall.ai - API for desktop recording
4| 
5| If you’re looking for a hosted desktop recording API, consider checking out [Recall.ai](https://www.recall.ai/product/desktop-recording-sdk/?utm_source=github&utm_medium=sponsorship&utm_campaign=recallai-github-sponsorship)
6| 
7| This project is sponsored by Recall.ai.
8| 
9| ---
10| 
11| > [!NOTE]  
12| > Use latest MacOS and Windows version, older versions have limited support
13| 
14| > [!NOTE]  
15| > During testing it wont answer if you ask something, you need to simulate interviewer asking question, which it will answer
16| 
17| A real-time AI assistant that provides contextual help during video calls, interviews, presentations, and meetings using screen capture and audio analysis.
18| 
19| ## Features
20| 
21| - **Live AI Assistance**: Real-time help powered by Google Gemini 2.0 Flash Live
22| - **Screen & Audio Capture**: Analyzes what you see and hear for contextual responses
23| - **Multiple Profiles**: Interview, Sales Call, Business Meeting, Presentation, Negotiation
24| - **Transparent Overlay**: Always-on-top window that can be positioned anywhere
25| - **Click-through Mode**: Make window transparent to clicks when needed
26| - **Cross-platform**: Works on macOS, Windows, and Linux (kinda, dont use, just for testing rn)
27| 
28| ## Setup
29| 
30| 1. **Get a Gemini API Key**: Visit [Google AI Studio](https://aistudio.google.com/apikey)
31| 2. **Install Dependencies**: `npm install`
32| 3. **Run the App**: `npm start`
| 
| ### OpenAI (secure main-process integration)
| 
| You can also enable OpenAI through the Electron main process (API key is never exposed to renderer code):
| 
| 1. Create a `.env` file in the project root:
|    ```bash
|    cp .env.example .env
|    ```
| 2. Add your key:
|    ```env
|    OPENAI_API_KEY=your_key_here
|    ```
| 3. Restart the app:
|    ```bash
|    npm start
|    ```
| 
| Security notes:
| - Never commit `.env`
| - Never paste API keys in renderer/localStorage
| - Keep all OpenAI calls in Electron main via IPC
33| 
34| ## Usage
35| 
36| 1. Enter your Gemini API key in the main window
37| 2. Choose your profile and language in settings
38| 3. Click "Start Session" to begin
39| 4. Position the window using keyboard shortcuts
40| 5. The AI will provide real-time assistance based on your screen and what interview asks
41| 
42| ## Keyboard Shortcuts
43| 
44| - **Window Movement**: `Ctrl/Cmd + Arrow Keys` - Move window
45| - **Click-through**: `Ctrl/Cmd + M` - Toggle mouse events
46| - **Close/Back**: `Ctrl/Cmd + \` - Close window or go back
47| - **Send Message**: `Enter` - Send text to AI
48| 
49| ## Audio Capture
50| 
51| - **macOS**: [SystemAudioDump](https://github.com/Mohammed-Yasin-Mulla/Sound) for system audio
52| - **Windows**: Loopback audio capture
53| - **Linux**: Microphone input
54| 
55| ## Requirements
56| 
57| - Electron-compatible OS (macOS, Windows, Linux)
| - Gemini API key
| - Screen recording permissions
| - Microphone/audio permissions
| - Optional: OpenAI API key via `.env`
